No it's not.

The character you start with only influences your chances of survivability
in a *very* minor way. NetHack is balanced in such a way that *every*
character is survivable.

You might start a wizard with a fully laden wand of wishing in the first
room, and think that this is a *very* survivable character, only to meet
the gnome with the wand of death in the next room.

On the other hand, a character with very low stats may find speed boots on
level three, and ascend.

Luck during the game is of much higher importance than one or two points
of dexterity at the start of the game. It's not as if it isn't easy to
increase most of your stats. Granted, intelligence is the most difficult
to increase, so if you're mostly playing wizards, you might disagree.

